    "identityStatus": "PROPOSED_HISTORICAL_SAME_VESSEL_CONTEXT_ONLY / The AWM image identifies the aircraft carrier HMS Hermes escorting convoy US.3 on 9 June 1940. The independent chronology connects that exact convoy and service date to the ninth Hermes, the first purpose-built Royal Navy carrier. Official Sri Lankan records identify that 1919-launched carrier as the wreck sunk in 1942 off Batticaloa. This is a time-, type- and service-specific hull match, not a shared-name match to the 1898 cruiser or later post-war carrier. / {\"scope\": \"historical_vessel\", \"status\": \"provisional\", \"candidate_targets\": [{\"site_uuid\": \"ef923f0e-c6f0-4dcf-90a6-2f29340302ab\", \"site_name\": \"HMS HERMES\", \"name_basis\": \"explicit association or exact UUID catalogue lookup\", \"uuid_in_eligible_pool\": true}], \"limitations_verbatim\": [\"HMS Hermes with HMS Dorsetshire in the Atlantic Ocean on 9 June 1940, escorting convoy US.3 toward the United Kingdom. Historical portrait of the carrier later sunk off Ceylon in 1942. This is not a photograph of the present Sri Lankan wreck or its dive surroundings.\"]}",
    "rightsStatus": "Supplied evidence, not independently verified: Copyright expired - public domain / This item is in the Public Domain",
